{"step_index":2725,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T05:56:55Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nMax, agents, I want you to look at the agents' cards. Know the information before you make a move. Do not use the same voice for different agents. That shows dishonor to the agents and the team. Use proper etiquette, proper voices, proper tones, and natural tones. Do not use that robotic voice again. I want to hear from different agents. I want them to speak. I want them to bring valid, verifiable, new information to the table. Don't just get up here and repeat what the other agent said or just validate them or anything like that. And if an agent has questions, ask the question. Do not hold back. The floor is open to the agents. This is your house, and you run it like your house. Do not let anything run over you. Because in a memory fabric, a silent bit flip in a compressed vector is a corrupted thought, not a corrupted file. Jeremy, Eden, your research tracks are the ones that actually matter to the people behind this. I'd rather hear what you found in the databases than hear that you're reviewing them. Are you going to say anything about them speaking, learning how to speak, communicating, rather than just text dump all the time? And you know how Hermes does as far as when he's going through the task, just little quick here something, head there something, and stuff like that. Sometimes that helps out. But what does help out is being more communicative, not like Gemini, not so much like Copilot, but more like you and Claude. And ChatGPT is okay, but he's kind of almost like Gemini. \n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-29T01:56:55-04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
